UID:SC-59C0AAC7-4EBE-4FD8-9E33-1011CCCE4D4B
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260825
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260826
SUMMARY:S: Call PRS — routing question\, not a third pitch
DESCRIPTION:*323.663.2167* — Tue–Fri 12–6. Decided 2026-08-24\; was due ~08
 -12.\n\nSequence so far: cold email 2026-03-13 (no reply) → real pitch 07-
 14\n(no reply) → one nudge 08-05 (no reply). `info@' has now died silently
 \n*three* times. Do NOT send a fourth email.\n\n*The ask is routing\, one 
 question:* who programs music and\nmoving-image work — Alex McDonald or Em
 ily Rose Epstein — and is that\nperson reachable directly.\n\n      Hi — m
 y name's Michael Webster. I sent a screening and\n      installation propo
 sal a few weeks back\, referred by the\n      Velaslavasay Panorama\, and 
 I just want to make sure it\n      reached the right person rather than ch
 ase it.  Who\n      handles programming for music and moving-image work — 
 Alex\n      or Emily?\n\n• *Don't re-pitch on the phone.* If they ask what
  it is\, one sentence:\n  an hour-long opera generated live by code\, a vo
 ice from a dead\n  planet.  Then back to the routing question.\n• *Best ou
 tcome:* a name and a direct address\, which converts the dead\n  `info@' t
 hread into a real one. *Second best:* "email info@ again" —\n  in which ca
 se ask whether it's worth resending\, and say the\n  Velaslavasay referral
  is in the subject line.\n• *Log the result here* (who answered\, name giv
 en\, any address) before\n  deciding the next move.
CATEGORIES:cal,org-calendar-staging
END:VEVENT
